      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! The answer is straightforward:\n\nAccording to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by **never loading it into the Hub process in the first place**. Instead:\n\n1. **A local secrets loader** reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. **The key is injected only into child-process environments** \u2014 specifically into the spawned Ingest agent and Query agent processes, immediately before they start\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** with the credential\n\nThis architecture ensures that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the API key simply by inspecting its own environment variables. The credential exists only transiently inside the short-lived child processes that actually need to call the Anthropic API.",
